---
STEP 0 — MANDATORY: call EnterPlanMode now, before anything else. If you cannot
enter plan mode (e.g. it is unavailable in this context), STOP and tell the user
to relaunch with:

    claude --permission-mode plan

Never begin execution from this command. This is Phase 1 of 2: read-only planning.

Inputs for this run:

    $ARGUMENTS

STEP 1 — Discovery (read-only). Delegate research to the `{{WF}}-planner`
subagent (its frontmatter sets `permissionMode: plan`, so it stays read-only).
Gather everything needed to produce a concrete plan.

STEP 2 — Present the plan. It MUST contain these literal sections:

    ## Steps              (ordered; the subagent + model tier per step)
    ## Agents             (roster; effort budget per agent)
    ## Files touched      (every file/dir to be created or modified)
    ## Commands           (every shell command class to be executed)
    ## Network & installs (explicit allowlist; empty means none permitted)
    ## Scope estimate     (size of change + token-cost class: 1x / ~4x / ~15x)

STEP 3 — On plan approval (the single human gate for this run):
  1. Create the `.workflow/` directory if absent.
  2. Write the approved plan verbatim to `.workflow/plan.md` with a first line
     `status: approved`.
  3. Write `.workflow/allowlist.txt` — one permitted network/install command
     pattern per line, taken ONLY from the plan's `## Network & installs`
     section. If none were approved, create the file empty.
  4. STOP and print the Phase 2 relaunch instructions:

         Plan approved and saved to .workflow/plan.md.
         To execute autonomously, relaunch in a fresh, isolated session:

             claude --dangerously-skip-permissions
             > /{{WF}}-execute

         (Alternative, keeps planning context at higher token cost:
             claude --continue --dangerously-skip-permissions )

         WARNING: run Phase 2 only inside a container, VM, or dedicated sandbox
         directory. See README-{{WF}}.md.
